Refuses an unqualified struct that two of the given packages both declare.

The generated change is scoped to one package clause, so there is a real choice
to make and no way to make it from source alone. Inferring one would retype the
wrong User; the message names the packages found and the target requalified.

-- args --
edit field User.ID --type UUID

-- want.error --
"User" is declared in packages [api store]; qualify field with the one you mean, as in "api.User.ID"

-- store/user.in.go --
package store

type User struct {
	ID string
}

-- api/user.in.go --
package api

type User struct {
	ID string
}
